  "notes": "{代|か}わる is an intransitive godan verb meaning for something to take the place of something else. The transitive pair is {代|か}える.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pair: {代|か}える (transitive — to substitute)\n- Pattern: AがBに{代|か}わる (A takes the place of B)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {代|か}わっている = has replaced, is acting as a substitute (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- AがBに{代|か}わる (A replaces B)\n- Aに{代|か}わって (in place of A, on behalf of A)\n- {代|か}わりに (instead, in place of — very common)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {代|か}わる: to take the place of, to be substituted (intransitive)\n- {変|か}わる: to change, to be altered (modification of state)\n- {換|か}わる / {替|か}わる: to be exchanged, to be swapped",
